# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets - never commit real credentials
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The optional integrations (assistant, music search, the Saudi National
# Address lookup) read their keys from a local .env. Only the example template
# is tracked.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
kaggle.json
# The canonical local secrets file is the root `.env` above. A file dropped
# there as bare `env` is not covered by the `env/` virtualenv rule below, which
# matches directories only, so guard the misnamed case explicitly.
/env

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Virtual environments
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
*/.venv/
# Suffixed environments at any depth. The production-pin compatibility env
# (model/DeBERTa-v3-xsmall/.venv-production/) is ignored by that directory's own
# .gitignore, but that file only exists on branches carrying the Model V2 work:
# checking out a branch without it exposed ~6,500 site-packages files as
# untracked. These root rules make suffixed envs ignored repo-wide regardless of
# which branch is checked out.
.venv-*/
venv-*/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python bytecode and build artifacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
*.pyd
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test, coverage, and type-checker caches
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.tox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
test-results/
test_output/
*.test.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs and local run output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/
runtime/
*.pid

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model caches and downloaded weights (models are vendored explicitly)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.cache/
.huggingface/
huggingface/
model_cache/
*.ort.cache

# Hugging Face cache created by the model/data dataset builders. Both notebooks
# default HF_HOME to "<cwd>/.pii_hf_cache", which holds multi-gigabyte source
# corpora (OpenPII 1.5M, Gretel, Nemotron) that are always re-downloadable.
.pii_hf_cache/

# Training checkpoints are regenerated by the training notebook and are large.
# The Model V1 (TinyBERT-4) FP32 ONNX and Hugging Face weights stay tracked on
# purpose: they are the previous generation's model of record, they cannot be
# rebuilt without retraining, and model/privacy_evaluation/privacy_eval/adapters.py
# loads the FP32 ONNX for the model-only evaluation arm.
model/TinyBERT-4/artifacts/tinybert_pii/checkpoints/

# The pinned Canary speech recogniser is acquired, never committed: it is a
# 700 MB third-party artifact that FullPipeline_V3/scripts/acquire_canary.py
# downloads and SHA-256 verifies on each device. Its manifest is tracked; the
# weights are not. The DeBERTa INT8 model *is* committed, because it is this
# project's own release artifact and the Pi cannot rebuild it.
*.nemo

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated PII corpora (model/data)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every corpus produced under model/ is a large local artifact regenerated from
# pinned sources plus committed metadata. Only the generators and their docs are
# tracked, so a new generated filename cannot be committed by accident.
model/data/*
!model/data/*.ipynb
!model/data/*.md
!model/data/.gitignore
!model/data/saudi_mena_pii_manifest.json
model/data/.*_execution.ipynb

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Captured audio and transcripts — never commit recorded speech
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.wav
*.flac
*.raw
moonshine_received_audio/
transcripts/

# The live pipeline stores raw *and* masked transcripts in a local SQLite
# database beside the app. Raw transcripts are exactly what this project exists
# to keep on the device, so they must never become a commit.
session_transcript.db
session_transcript.db-*
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Except the audio benchmark fixtures. They are not recorded speech: the
# privacy clips are Piper TTS output of sentences written for this project with
# entirely fictional PII, and the public clips are verbatim LibriSpeech
# dev-clean (CC BY 4.0). Full_Pipeline_Audio_Benchmark.py needs them on the
# Raspberry Pi, which has no TTS and no dataset download, so they are committed
# and their SHA-256 is pinned in audio_benchmark.manifest.json.
!model/privacy_evaluation/fixtures/audio_benchmark/clips/*.wav

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Jupyter
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor and OS files
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Contents, not the directory itself: git does not descend into an ignored
# directory, so `.vscode/` would make the negation below unreachable.
.vscode/*
# Except the shared path configuration: the notebooks import local OnKith
# modules by bare name after adding three directories to sys.path, and Pylance
# needs the same three paths to agree with the runtime. That is project setup,
# not a personal editor preference.
!.vscode/settings.json
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local scratch
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ad-hoc evaluation dumps kept on the development machine only.
/historic/
